      "side": 1,
      "message": "minor: I was looking at the mmio range considered by hypervisor and noticed that `pkvm_ramoops_console_pa` would also be considered mmio range as its reserved in E820. If my understanding is correct, its currently `PKVM_PAGE_OWNED` and mapped as `PAGE_KERNEL`, but shared with pKVM(in `create_hyp_mmu`). With this change, `pkvm_host_donate_hyp_mmio` if invoked for ramoops range will re-map it as `PAGE_KERNEL_IO_NOCACHE` as it is considered mmio range. Not sure if its a big problem. And `pkvm_hyp_mmu_map` ultimately calls `hyp_mmu_flush_tlb` which BUG()s. \n\nWe could probably mark `pkvm_ramoops_console_pa` as `PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_OWNED` so that `pkvm_host_donate_hyp_mmio` will reject the donation?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "c9a0ff4a_398c7d7c",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tu64 prot \u003d (u64)pgprot_val(PAGE_KERNEL_IO_NOCACHE);\n\n\tif (phys \u003d\u003d pkvm_ramoops_console_pa)\n\t\tprot \u003d (u64)pgprot_val(PAGE_KERNEL);\n\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c",
